  "worked_solution": "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a *single step* of a numerical method, when the step begins from an *exact value*. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+\u0394x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+\u0394y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the LTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- After the first step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.22$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.117.$ So, the LTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{1} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.22)-1.117 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1.22}-1.117 \\\\  & \u2248-0.012.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the second step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.44$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.185.$ So, the LTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{2} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.44)-1.185 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1.44}-1.185 \\\\  & =0.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the third step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.66$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.299.$ So, the LTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{3} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.66)-1.299 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1.66}-1.299 \\\\ = & \u2248-0.011.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | $x$ | $y$ | ${\u03c4}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1.000$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.22$ | $1.117$ | $-0.012$ |\n| $2$ | $0.44$ | $1.185$ | $0.015$ |\n| $3$ | $0.66$ | $1.299$ | $-0.011$ |",
